    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-duplicate (\"possible duplicate\") detection for owner creation. When a new owner is not a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a different telephone, it is still created and now reports `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id; otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added two read-only fields to the `Owner` schema: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32). These generate the corresponding `OwnerDto` accessors, and MapStruct auto-maps them from the `Owner` entity by name.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added persisted `possibleDuplicate` (`Boolean`) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (`Integer`) columns with getters/setters, so the values computed at create time survive to the `GET` read-back.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after the hard-duplicate identity check passes, it computes the soft-match via a new `findPossibleDuplicate(owner)` helper and stores the result on the owner before saving.\n- **`findPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 returns the oldest existing owner (lowest id) that matches `lastName` (case-insensitively) and `postcode` while carrying a *different* normalized telephone; returns `null` when the owner has no postcode or no such match. The controller sets `possibleDuplicate` from whether that id is non-null.\n- **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` and `possible_duplicate_of` columns to the `owners` table so the entity maps cleanly across all supported databases (tests run on hsqldb).\n\nThe logic sits after `rejectDuplicateIdentity`, so it only ever flags owners that were accepted (i.e., genuinely not hard duplicates), matching the spec's \"not a hard duplicate but shares\u2026\" wording.",
